<article class="env-definition" id="F38374">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/F38374">Definition <span data-tag="F38374">8.3.2.7</span>.</a> Let $F: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be a functor between ordinary categories. We will say that $F$ is a <em>quasi-fibration</em> if, for every object $C \in \calC $ and every isomorphism $f: F(X) \rightarrow Y$ in $\calD $, there exists an isomorphism $\overline{f}: X \rightarrow \overline{Y}$ in $\calC $ such that $F( \overline{f} ) = f$. </p>
